Message-ID: <AANLkTikdusyDDkFNknyzQgSZbFoh1hSG4W-g3spnq=hQ@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Jennie,

My guess is that Amelia can handle this situation, but you may need to
take a look at the covariates you are including in the imputation. The
error messages about non-positive definite matrices usually mean that
the data is not of full rank. This usually is because there are two
variables in your data that are linear transformations of each other
or an exhaustive set of dummy variables. Once you get rid of any of
these types of problems, you should be able to proceed with Amelia!

Good luck,
matt.

